    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 the only test in the suite is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that on a successful owner create, an audit line be emitted via the logger named `AUDIT` containing the owner id, the `customerCode`, and the `registrationDate`.\n\nI implemented this in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n- Added a dedicated SLF4J logger `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`.\n- After `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (so the owner id is assigned), emit:\n  ```\n  AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n  ```\n\nThe line is emitted only on the successful path, after all rejection rules and derived-field assignment, and carries the id, the derived `customerCode`, and the adjusted `registrationDate` (whose `LocalDate.toString()` matches the ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` value the test reads back from `GET /api/owners/{id}`). The `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` check and the full suite pass.",
